This is an independent Rust implementation, not a port of existing code: the
inference engine was written from scratch against ONNX Runtime. The per-file
copyright headers state the same.


MODEL OWNERSHIP

The models this project converts and runs are not ours, and converting a model
does not change its licence or its ownership.

  - GLiNER2 is developed by Fastino (https://fastino.ai). See arXiv:2507.18546.
    The weights this engine loads originate from https://huggingface.co/fastino
    and remain subject to the licence their publisher sets. Check it before
    redistributing them with an application.

  - GLiNER (Generalist Model for Named Entity Recognition), the line these
    models descend from, is the work of Urchade Zaratiana et al.
    See arXiv:2311.08526.

  - No model weights are distributed from this repository. The ONNX exports
    published under https://huggingface.co/jugaadsrl are derived artefacts of
    upstream checkpoints and carry their licence; the conversion adds no
    ownership claim over the model.

  - The conversion scripts under onnx_conversion_scripts/ operate on those
    upstream models and produce derived artefacts. Converting a model does not
    change its licence.

This project implements inference for those models and claims no ownership
over them. What is ours is the engine, the exporters and the tests.


